But note: containers that recurse and produce empty entries are effectively equal. For dicts with the same keys where each value is deeply strictly equal → recursion produces []. Good.

For lists of the same length where each item is deeply strictly equal → []. Good.

Container kind matching: both dicts → recurse; both lists → recurse. Otherwise if not strictly equal → `~`.

Also: what if both sides are the same kind of container and equal? Recursion returns [] — good.

What about equal scalars of the same type → no entry.

